# Impeccable design-tool working dir (critique snapshots, screenshots, caches, live config).
# Canonical PRODUCT.md / DESIGN.md live at the app root and stay tracked.
.impeccable/

# Client-handover material: kept on disk, never tracked. The sign-off documents
# are delivered to the client as rendered documents under the contract, not as
# files in a repository — and the repository itself is handed over as a fresh
# single-commit export, which must not carry them. Screenshots are additionally
# large PNGs with no business in git history.
docs/client-handover/

# Superseded design plans: kept on disk as the project's own working record, but
# not tracked. They are development history with no operational value to anyone
# receiving this codebase, and they carry developer identities and throwaway test
# credentials that should not travel with a handover.
docs/plans/_archive/

# Manual test plans: point-in-time QA records for work already shipped, kept on
# disk as the project's own record. Same reasoning as docs/plans/_archive/.
docs/test-plans/
